== template color` is false; markers are all `hsep`.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/20/code.py:61:#    - Across samples, the same marker color leads to different templates, so a human can reject\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/20/code.py:69:#    - The marker color is always the horizontal separator color and is excluded from template\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/20/code.py:261:    repeated divider/marker color, while the per-column vertical separator colors are the true lookup\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c416de3/13/code.py:448:      inward diagonal cell. Those marker colors are the colors to use when the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/7/code.py:42:# - Only three marker colors are introduced and each has a single clear role:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/7/code.py:59:#   false here; the solver must instead find explicit start/end marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/7/code.py:247:    assert len(hits) == 1, f\\\"expected exactly one block containing marker color {color}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/17/code.py:12:# - Small-example intuition: if the legend says red=up and blue=right, a train whose marker colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/17/code.py:14:#   and marker colors, while the vacated source and every intermediate slide position become a solid\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/17/code.py:20:# - Hidden assumptions audited: the original solver assumed marker colors were stripe colors and that\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/17/code.py:207:    - Read the corner legend, rotate/flip the train so its marker colors lie on their legend-coded sides relative\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:22:#    - Original 65b59efc: marker color directly names the template, and the marker's local\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:35:#        (2,0). The key difference is \\\"match border colors across bands, ignore marker color\\\".\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:42:#    - `marker color == template color` is false.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:52:#    - Across examples, the same marker color appears under multiple different outputs, which makes\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:53:#      \\\"marker color chooses template\\\" visibly fail.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:61:#    - Inputs are constructed so the original rule cannot succeed: marker color equals the global\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:232:    Decode a stamped legend where marker color is a decoy and the usable key lives on colored borders.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D9/1/code.py:143:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/16/code.py:95:    Key insight: marker color and local marker coordinates still decode template choice and block position, but the final canvas is cropped by the set of occupied slots, not by rendered foreground pixels, because empty blocks now carry their own visible default pattern.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/16/code.py:142:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/15/code.py:84:    - Match each train to the station group of the same color, then rotate/flip so the train's marker colors face the same-color borders of that station's region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/15/code.py:717:    assert fallback, \\\"region must provide at least one required marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c416de3/6/code.py:16:#   TL source pattern A copies only to BR using BR's marker color; TR source pattern B\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c416de3/6/code.py:17:#   copies only to BL using BL's marker color. The two targets therefore complete with\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c416de3/6/code.py:63:#   exemplars; target outputs still use the target corner's own marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c416de3/6/code.py:263:      diagonal while keeping its own local marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/9/code.py:171:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/20/code.py:77:#   without couplers). No rule depends on hidden color ordering; marker colors are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/20/code.py:589:    - The combo still resolves each true pair by “coupler count picks the station, marker colors fix the orientation”, but now that logic must be applied only after filtering out the fake train and fake station and after decoding the cross-shaped divider geometry.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c416de3/14/code.py:322:        assert ctrl_color == tcol, f\\\"target {c_key} control color {ctrl_color} != marker color {tcol}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:7:#   The middle band may contain marker colors red/green/yellow with global counts 3, 4, 5, but those\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:16:#   1. `marker color == template color` no longer holds. Marker colors are sampled from colors not used\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:18:#   2. `each tile column is monochrome` no longer holds. A physical column may carry several marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:26:#   3. Each marker color appears in at least two physical columns, and at least two physical columns are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:33:#   3. Exactly K marker colors appear in the middle band: enforced by allocating one global count group\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:70:    template choice is recovered from a global count-order correspondence between marker colors and template sizes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/2/code.py:32:#    Removing marker colors actually simplifies the scene: regions and trains are still readable, and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/6/code.py:34:#      any single template color, marker color, or palette swatch color. The generator enforces that.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/6/code.py:145:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/1/code.py:64:#    - main() assumes the marker color forms exactly one meaningful corner component.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/1/code.py:65:#      generate_input() uses marker color only for that shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/1/code.py:159:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/21/code.py:24:#      2. Read middle-band markers; marker color chooses the template.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/21/code.py:189:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/21/code.py:256:    - Rows N+1..2N hold marker pixels; each tile column still uses exactly one marker color, but\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/21/code.py:267:    Key insight: The marker colors still tell you \\\"which stamp\\\", but the marker positions no longer\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/28/code.py:26:#    Fused: the shared wall segment is drawn in one dedicated marker color instead.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/28/code.py:37:#    - One global marker color is used, not a different mixed color per pair.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/28/code.py:59:#    - Noise never uses the marker color, and noise is not allowed to overwrite marker cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/16/code.py:169:    - A candidate is valid only when the transformed two-coupler line has the same horizontal/vertical orientation as the candidate station and every marker color points toward the matching boundary stripe of that station's region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/30/code.py:31:#   tile column contains only one marker color. Distinct template/palette sets and large numbers\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/30/code.py:231:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/19/code.py:77:    - The middle band (between the two separator rows) contains marker pixels; marker color still identifies a template, and local marker coordinates still identify an output block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/19/code.py:102:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/19/code.py:322:    # Keep template/marker colors disjoint from palette colors so the recoloring rule\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/2/code.py:55:#   treats every non-background, non-corner-marker color as \\\"wallish\\\" when finding\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/4/code.py:53:    - Rows N+1..2N hold sparse marker pixels; each tile column still uses one marker color only.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/4/code.py:112:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:11:#      2. A middle-band marker pixel uses that same template color, so marker color directly reveals j.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:25:#        A marker colored 6 therefore chooses the template whose top-band color is 2, and the output block keeps\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:28:#    - Palette colors are sampled distinct and disjoint from template colors, so marker colors visibly belong to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:35:#    - Original `j = tcol_to_j[v]` is invalid: marker color v is now a palette color, not a template color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:49:#    - Humans can see that middle-band marker colors do not occur in the top templates but do occur in the bottom\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:58:#    - One marker color per middle tile column is preserved, avoiding clutter in the marker band.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:63:#    - main() assumes palette colors are unique so `marker color -> palette entry` is unambiguous; generator\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:109:    - The middle band (rows N+1..2N) contains sparse marker pixels. Each physical tile column uses one marker color, but that color is a palette code rather than a template color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:114:    - To decide which template to stamp, first match the marker color to a palette entry, then use the template-color key inside that same palette pair to identify the corresponding top-band template.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:117:    Key insight: the output template is recovered by a three-step indirection chain `marker color -> palette pair -> template color key -> top template`, and the palette color itself never appears in the output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:172:    # Read markers; marker color names a palette entry, local position names the output block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:183:                assert tile_marker is None or v == tile_marker, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/14/code.py:184:                assert v in marker_to_j, \\\"marker color must match one palette code\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D10/1/code.py:225:    - Every side gap emits a beam in the marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:8:#    Original task used marker color -> template index directly, then palette column j -> template j.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:9:#    Here the chain is two-step and indirect: marker color matches a palette swatch color, and that swatch's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:12:#    are [C,B,A]. A marker colored A selects T0, even though A appears under the rightmost palette column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:18:#    - `tcol_to_j[v]` no longer works because marker colors are palette colors, not template colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:25:#    Humans can match marker colors to the bottom swatches because those colors never appear in the top templates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:51:    Decode a tiled legend where marker colors point to palette swatches, then reverse that palette order to recover templates.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:56:    - Middle band (rows N+1..2N): sparse marker pixels; each tile column uses a single marker color, but that color comes from the palette band rather than the template band.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:61:    - To decide which template to stamp, first match the marker color to a palette swatch color, then map that swatch's reversed palette position back to its template.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:105:    # Middle band: marker color identifies the logical palette entry, not the template color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:117:                assert tile_marker is None or v == tile_marker, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/5/code.py:118:                assert v in marker_to_template, \\\"marker color must match a palette swatch color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/12/code.py:26:#      blue, so local slot (lr, lc) only tells us where to stamp and marker color tells us which template.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/12/code.py:27:#    - Fused task here: the same physical tile column can contain several marker colors at once, and that\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/12/code.py:50:#    - Original assumption \\\"one tile column has one marker color\\\" is false. The new solver must inspect\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/12/code.py:114:    Decode a tiled stamp legend where mixed marker colors share columns and column position controls flips.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/12/code.py:127:    Key insight: marker color and marker column now carry different pieces of information: color picks the template, while physical column picks the flip operation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/28/code.py:48:#    - Original assumption \\\"each middle tile column has one uniform marker color\\\" is false. Used columns may\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D2/0/code.py:53:#     - Choosing the most frequent non-bg, non-marker color as the wall color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D2/0/code.py:167:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/13/code.py:200:    - Within that recovered core, marker color still chooses the template, marker local coordinates still\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/13/code.py:230:                assert tile_color is None or v == tile_color, \\\"tile column must have uniform marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/8/code.py:40:#    The fusion adds no extra marker colors; it reuses the original palette and only changes motion.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:34:#         - one embedded marker color, drawn only on background holes of that shown template\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:35:#      4. Embedded marker colors are palette colors, not template colors. A marker's color must be matched\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:50:#    - The new cue is repeated K times per sample: every top tile contains a marker color and every palette\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:53:#    - The marker colors are drawn only from the K palette colors, while template colors are chosen from a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:61:#    - `marker color == template color` is false. Marker colors now belong to the bottom palette set.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:65:#    - \\\"a marker tile stamps the template shown in that same tile\\\" is false. The marker color determines the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:94:#      embedded marker color inside the palette set; the generator enforces both conditions and gives every tile\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:96:#    - main() assumes each palette color appears once in the top band as a marker color; the generator uses a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:316:      * the embedded marker color that matches one bottom palette swatch\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/23/code.py:318:      that marker color, recolored with that same palette color, into output block (lr, lc).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D2/1/code.py:114:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/13/code.py:234:    # Score one rigid transform by asking whether every marker color ends up\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/13/code.py:615:    - A transform is valid only when all marker colors face the matching boundary stripes of that station's region and the transformed coupler shape matches that station's oriented 2-cell line exactly.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/1/code.py:52:# - Wall detection relied on \\\"most frequent non-bg, non-marker color\\\". This also\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/1/code.py:53:#   still holds because the input still contains only bg / wall / marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D10/1/code.py:157:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/22/code.py:44:#        marker local slot = (2, 0), marker color = 8\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/22/code.py:64:#    - \\\"Marker color alone completely determines output repainting\\\" is false; marker color now works\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/22/code.py:91:#    - main() assumes each marker column is color-uniform and that the marker color matches exactly one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/22/code.py:275:    - The marker color identifies which template/legend stack to use. The template key color is the unique\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_com