ode_combo/e12f9a14/42/code.py:464:    - When two beams reach the same background cell on the same tick, that cell is repainted with a fixed special marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D4/0/code.py:123:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D1/0/code.py:234:    Inflate the frame layout and fill each slot with the piece that shares its wall-marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D1/0/code.py:255:        assert color in piece_by_color, \\\"every slot marker color must have a matching piece\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/32/code.py:370:    - The real inference is two-layered: first partition the source colors into the two visible families {blue, green} and {red, yellow}, then map same-family vs different-family collisions to two distinct marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:166:      monochrome rectangular frame whose outer border also contains one marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D4/1/code.py:44:#    - Original wall inference \\\"most frequent non-bg non-marker color\\\" still works because the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:21:#   marker colors define the pairing.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:59:#   fixed-position marker color instead.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:76:# - A human can see the same top-left marker color repeated once on a frame and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:92:#   visible equality of marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:100:# - Every frame and sprite has exactly one top-left marker, and marker colors are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:104:# - For each pair, marker color differs from both the frame body color and the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:113:    Pair scattered sprites to grid frames by a shared corner-marker color, then\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:120:      corner. Matching pairs share that marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:126:      fixed top-left marker color of each object.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:127:    - Match each frame to the sprite with the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:134:    - The same corner-marker color explains the pairing, and the matched pair\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/1/code.py:241:N_RANGE = (2, 3)  # keep total pair count low enough to give marker colors a clean disjoint palette\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/0/code.py:40:#    - Wall-color inference by \\\"most frequent non-bg, non-marker color\\\" remains valid because the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/0/code.py:145:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/3/code.py:33:      same marker color has more visible weight on thick sides than on thin sides.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/3/code.py:74:    - `frame_color = border majority` is unsafe if border pixels include marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/3/code.py:94:    - The same four marker colors reappear across many objects, which encourages reading\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/3/code.py:103:      is different from all four shared marker colors; this keeps extraction clean within\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/3/code.py:122:    - assumption: every side band contains exactly one marker color in addition to the base\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/3/code.py:400:      changes the visible weight of marker colors, so the solver must interpret edge markers\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D3/2/code.py:30:    new_layout: each slot is filled by its own unique marker color inside the frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D3/2/code.py:81:      the generator guarantees frame-color cells outnumber any marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D3/2/code.py:168:    - Inner walls use the frame color; each slot region is a solid unique marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D2/1/code.py:45:      many pieces contain the same green marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/39/code.py:31:# - A single shared marker color is used for all targets. This prevents the task\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/39/code.py:58:#   shared marker color attached just outside it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/39/code.py:59:# - Because the marker color is reused across all targets, the only stable pairing cue\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/39/code.py:72:#   pair, while one distinct shared marker color identifies all receiver endpoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/39/code.py:254:    assert len(marker_colors) == 1, \\\"expected one shared marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/1/code.py:141:    assert len(unique_cols) == 1, \\\"expected exactly one unique non-background marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/1/code.py:145:    assert len(marker_locs) == 1, \\\"marker color must occupy exactly one cell\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:47:#    - Original wall-color inference excluded one marker color by identity, which still\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:49:#      marker color as the only non-background color whose every pixel lies on the grid\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:109:    - Detect the border-only marker color, then launch one flood-fill from all of its pixels at once.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:130:    assert len(marker_candidates) == 1, \\\"expected exactly one repeated border-only marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D15/2/code.py:135:    assert other_cols, \\\"no non-background non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/9/code.py:27:#   stable marker color (red). There are only 2-3 true gaps, but 3-5 same-color distractor diagonals,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/9/code.py:32:#   avoid marker neighborhoods. The solver assumes exactly one fg color plus one marker color, true gaps\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/9/code.py:58:    - bg is the dominant color. One non-bg color is the line network; red is the marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:20:    - The marker color equals the color of the outside piece that belongs to that hole.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:21:    - Therefore shape finds the candidate set, and marker color resolves duplicate-shape ambiguity.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:26:      adding the touching marker color makes the match unique.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:60:  - Colors do not undergo arbitrary remapping. The marker color is copied directly from the corresponding piece.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:64:  - Each hole has at most one non-frame marker color in its 4-neighborhood.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:65:  - For repeated non-unit shapes, piece color equals the hole's marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code.py:107:    - Shape still determines geometric fit; marker color breaks ties among repeated shapes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D15/0/code