rs from the marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/0/code.py:57:    Key insight: Coupler count still picks the target and marker colors still fix the orientation, but the final body color now comes from whichever stripe color occupies the most boundary area around the destination region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/24/code.py:82:    - No extra marker colors are introduced. The destination uses only background plus\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/1/code.py:11:#       body color instead of its minority marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/1/code.py:13:#     - Each multi-color sprite still has one large body color and one small marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/1/code.py:24:#     - When multiple anchors exist, marker colors often reuse a different anchor color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/1/code.py:176:    - Interior sprites are multi-color components with a dominant body color and a minority marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:12:#    8 swaps with one distinguished marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:13:# b) The distinguished marker color must be visible from the input, so each train is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:25:# g) The solver assumes a unique most frequent marker color exists on every train;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:44:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Swap train body color 8 with the designated marker color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:54:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return the unique most frequent marker color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:56:    assert counts, \\\"Expected at least one marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:58:    assert len(top) == 1 or top[0][1] > top[1][1], \\\"Expected a unique repeated marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:71:    - Each train also has stripe-colored marker pixels, with one marker color repeated twice.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:76:    - Choose the rotation/flip whose marker colors face the same-colored boundary stripes of the target region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D5/3/code.py:78:    - If the chosen docking transform includes a vertical flip, swap body color 8 with the repeated marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/22/code.py:66:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Marker bars are thin 4-connected components of the given marker color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/3/code.py:9:#       a minority-color marker, and that marker color selected one isolated border anchor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/3/code.py:20:#       original logic would ask which marker color matches which anchor color;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/3/code.py:35:#     - Old component filtering kept any component whose marker color existed among anchors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/3/code.py:36:#       That is now invalid because marker colors are intentionally unrelated to anchor colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/3/code.py:86:    Key insight: The task no longer matches marker color to anchor color; the correspondence\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/41/code.py:80:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Marker bars are thin 4-connected components of the given marker color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D2/3/code.py:50:#    The variant is inferable from examples because marker colors stop carrying information:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/6/code.py:73:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Marker bars are thin 4-connected components of the given marker color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/14/code.py:82:    Marker bars are thin 4-connected components of the given marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/14/code.py:355:    # Reserve marker colors 2/3 and grey 5 for lane-role semantics so examples stay legible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D16/1/code.py:64:    - Interior connected sprites use one body color plus a rarer marker color; optional singleton sprites still exist.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D16/1/code.py:68:    - Match each movable sprite to the anchor with the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/12/code.py:77:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Marker bars are thin 4-connected components of the given marker color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/15/code.py:85:#       paired training frames: guaranteed by structured placement and unique marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/9/code.py:91:#        * single-cell marker color depends on how many triangles aim at that empty cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/9/code.py:205:    - Orientation still tells you where every projectile lands, but two different aggregations are now needed afterward: compare shooter team against the hit sprite's team for sprite damage, and count how many shooters share an empty landing cell for the collision marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/10/code.py:63:#    No extra marker colors are introduced. The dst prefill uses the same two\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D16/2/code.py:21:#     - Example: a 5-cell sprite with marker color 4 wants to slide right until its marker column matches\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D16/2/code.py:56:#     - Every movable component still has either a least-frequent marker color matching an anchor or is a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D16/2/code.py:88:    - Match each sprite to the border anchor with the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ce