 of colors, and the marker colors come only\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D16/2/code.py:50:#    from those visible pairs. Humans can match marker colors back to stripe\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D16/2/code.py:101:    - For the target region, interpret each marker color through the bordering\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D16/2/code.py:109:    from stripe-pattern decoding: the marker color identifies a boundary side\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/1/code.py:50:#   - align-marker colors are chosen outside the anchor-color set when possible, making the role split visible\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/22/code.py:229:        assert color in {t1_color, t2_color}, \\\"marker color must match tile1 or tile2\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/22/code.py:282:      * each marker color equals either tile1's foreground color or tile2's foreground color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/22/code.py:288:    - For each quadrant independently, compare its corner marker color to tile1/tile2.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7491f3cf/22/code.py:294:    - The output is a four-way local mosaic: marker colors do not choose one global \\\"inside\\\" side,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:14:#      The marker colors are the pairing key. The fill color of the `src` cavity is still what\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:20:#      Variant logic must place red into top-left and blue into bottom-right by marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:28:#    - Cavity count is reduced from 4-9 to 4-5 so we can afford unique marker colors without\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:35:#      pixel. The new solver explicitly separates majority fill color from minority marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:53:#    - Marker colors and fill colors are disjoint palettes. The human can infer: \\\"same marker color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:63:#      one majority fill color and one single-pixel marker color. Generator guarantee: yes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:64:#    - Each `dst` hole has exactly one adjacent non-outline marker color. Generator guarantee: yes,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:82:    Fill `dst` holes using the fill color of the `src` cavity that shares the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D3/0/code.py:28:#    - Old orientation search scored marker colors against boundary stripe colors. That assumption is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/3/code.py:18:#     matching marker color to anchor color, but the solver has to keep 8-connected components intact and must\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/3/code.py:66:    - Each interior sprite is an 8-connected multicolor component: one body color plus one 1-pixel marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/3/code.py:70:    - Pair every sprite with the isolated border anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D11/3/code.py:17:#   diagonal directions as in the original task, and place one special marker color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D11/3/code.py:19:# - The marker color is fixed across the whole task: 9. It is reserved from the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D11/3/code.py:31:#     cell on the boundary is changed, and it is changed to marker color 9.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D11/3/code.py:37:# - A fixed marker color keeps the new rule learnable from a few examples.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D11/3/code.py:53:#   endpoint and then writes the marker color there.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D11/3/code.py:71:# - Because the marker color is constant and introduced only in the 