olors are the symbolic codes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/2/code.py:58:#    all anchor/marker colors, which makes the marker pixel visually salient instead of blending into\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/2/code.py:72:    - One corner contains a compact framed legend whose inner rows encode [anchor color, marker color].\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/2/code.py:73:    - Elsewhere, isolated border pixels are anchors and interior multi-color sprites carry the marker colors from the legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/2/code.py:80:    Key insight: The edge position still chooses the translation axis, but color matching is no longer direct — the corner legend translates marker colors into anchor colors first.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D14/0/code.py:9:#   orientation was recovered by asking which transformed marker colors faced matching boundary\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D14/0/code.py:12:#   relative to the body centroid supplies a second orthogonal direction. Example: a marker colored\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D14/0/code.py:282:        # - marker color -> the transformed body-to-marker attachment direction\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D14/0/code.py:299:        assert len(orth_dirs) == 1, \\\"Variant generator must give each marker color a unique orthogonal mate\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/7/code.py:11:#    Example with template blocks [A][B][A], marker color A, and step budget 12:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/32/code.py:57:  - Once grouping is spatial, marker color cannot identify a square group anymore. The solver instead assumes there is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/32/code.py:81:    so the solver cannot mistake the marker color for a group-color key.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D12/3/code.py:55:#    Colors keep their original role onl