 and keeps\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D7/0/code.py:85:    four-way divider frame determines the final orientation because marker colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:155:    - Non-marker colors appear as one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical line fragments.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:172:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:183:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:32:# - Template colors are sampled without repetition, and marker colors are chosen\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:64:#   scanning, so the template rule has a real effect once the marker color fixes the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/8/code.py:17:#   the ordered pair of marker colors to orient it so marker 5 is at the output\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/8/code.py:37:#   rectangular, its two unique marker colors sit on the same edge, and the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/8/code.py:317:    assert set(pos) == {MARKER_TL, MARKER_TR}, \\\"anchor must contain exactly the two marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:88:    - Interior sprites are multi-color connected components; each has a rare marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:92:    - Pair each sprite with the border segment whose color matches the sprite marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/21/code.py:354:    assert len(set(colors)) >= 2, \\\"marker colors must expose multiple cycle phases\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:317:    - Non-marker colors form thin horizontal/vertical stroke fragments that may now include same-color T or + junctions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d