s both order and rotation codes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/2/code.py:328:    - Extract the four pieces and read each piece's unique marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/2/code.py:329:    - Sort pieces by marker color ascending; this fixes their output corner order:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/2/code.py:335:    - The same visible marker color carries two instructions at once: it says which\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:20:#     objects: 1-cell-thick rectilinear polylines of 3-4 non-marker colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:214:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:223:    assert marker_colors <= KNOWN_MARKERS, f\\\"unexpected marker colors: {marker_colors}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:226:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:66:    - The border contains one non-corner anchor pixel for each marker color; those anchor pixels may touch other non-background border decorations.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:70:    - For each movable interior component, use its marker color to find the border pixel of the same color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:75:    - Isolation is no longer the signal for anchors. The stable cue is that marker colors point to unique border pixels, and the edge containing that border pixel determines the slide axis.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:90:    # --- STEP 1) Read candidate marker colors from interior multi-color sprites. ---\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/16/code.py:69:#      body color plus connector/marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/36/code.py:161:    - Azure squares are still processed by increasing input column and stacked on the left; red squares are processed by decreasing input column and stacked on the right.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:40:#   marker colors and asserts that each marker component is a domino.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:142:    - Non-marker colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical stroke fragments.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:159:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:164:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected at least one marker color\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:169:        assert comps, \\\"marker color must have at least one component\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:173:            assert axis is not None, f\\\"marker color {marker_color} must form domino components\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/37/code.py:20:#        * the center cell of each block in marker color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/37/code.py:26:#        * D1/1: source cells are identified by marker color, not by being the lone rare pattern.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/37/code.py:33:#        * 2-3 marked centers prove the marker color is a class-level cue, not a singleton.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/37/code.py:64:#    - The marker color has exactly one role: \\\"this active center cell is a template anchor\\\".\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/37/code.py:150:    - There are 2-3 identical marked template cells whose active pixels use one marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b99e7126/37/code.py:155:    - Find the marker color by looking for the less frequent non-majority color, and collect all\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/2/code.py:21:#    - Example trace: with H=12, marker color 4, sprite marker at (7, 3), and anchor at (1, 8),\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/2/code.py:64:    - Match each sprite to the secondary-ring anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/2/code.py:133:        # --- STEP 3) Decide marker color for this component. ---\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:75:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by reinterpreting one shared marker color as either a missing bend cell or an arm-side redirection control.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:90:    Key insight: The marker color no longer tells you its job. The local geometry does: embedded bend markers restore missing corners, while offset single-neighbor markers flip an arm and force a new boundary-reaching ray.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:97:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:108:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/23/code.py:204:    - Azure squares are processed by increasing input column and placed toward the left side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/10/code.py:28:#   8-connected components, detects per-component singleton marker colors, sorts\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/10/code.py:343:    - Extract the four connected pieces and sort them by marker color: 5 first, then 6, then 8, and finally the unmarked piece.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/10/code.py:349:    - The singleton marker colors no longer just identify an anchor; together they encode the assembly sequence, and the absence of a marker encodes the \\\"do not rotate\\\" exception.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:26:#      one marker color from the region and says \\\"start the boundary band with this\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:361:    - One wall cell next to each region is recolored as a clue dot; that dot repeats one marker color from the adjacent region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:364:    - Recover the true wall mask structurally, then for each region sort its internal marker colors by boundary distance and prepend the base color if the first marker starts deeper than distance 0.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:390:# ---- Distinct marker colors across the whole grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/19/code.py:34:#      anchor uses a marker color.  This variant extracts 8-connected pieces.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/19/code.py:57:#    - Exactly one piece contains the singleton marker color 5.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/0/code.py:428:    - Any color whose 4-connected components are all singletons is a marker color rather than a line color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/0/code.py:444:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/0/code.py:455:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:20:#       deepest marker color C, so the solver can infer both spiral start/direction and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:316:    - The same corner also has a short inward diagonal of distinct marker colors, ordered from shallow to deeper Chebyshev depths.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:320:    - Read the diagonal marker colors by increasing depth, reverse that list, then append the region base color to complete the repeating palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D13/1/code.py:49:#    flag. The same marker color appears in both partitions, so a human solver can\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D13/1/code.py:61:    Slide interior sprites toward the border anchor that matches both their marker color and their background partition.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D13/1/code.py:70:    - Match a sprite to the anchor of the same marker color inside that same region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D13/1/code.py:73:    Key insight: marker color is no longer a global key because colors can repeat across the two background regions; region membership plus anchor side determines the move.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/29/code.py:83:#     - colors keep structural roles only; the marker color reuses one motif color, but\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/5/code.py:140:    assert marker_cells, \\\"marker color 5 must appear\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/8/code.py:328:    - For every region, sort marker colors by boundary depth to build its palette, prepending the region base color when the shallowest marker is not on depth 0.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/8/code.py:354:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:93:    - The grid has one dominant background and several non-marker colors that form thin orthogonal line fragments.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:94:    - Any foreground color whose 4-connected components are all singleton pixels acts as a marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:110:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:121:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/18/code.py:76:#   - The marker color is fixed across examples, and the generator enforces both marked and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/18/code.py:110:#     becomes the fixed marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/18/code.py:111:#   - Because input fg/bg vary but the marker color stays fixed, humans can infer that the third\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/18/code.py:251:    - Recolor only the matched window's scene-foreground cells to a fixed third marker color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/24/code.py:228:    - Inside the chosen region, order marker colors by boundary distance to form the palette, prepending the base color if the shallowest marker is not on the boundary.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/24/code.py:259:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:147:    - Non-marker colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical polyline fragments that may cross.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:165:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:176:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/1/code.py:70:#   - Distinct marker colors within a region stay few and ordered by visible path\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/0/code.py:83:    - Match each sprite to the anchor sharing its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/27/code.py:44:#      one border marker color).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/27/code.py:61:#    - Crop colors are sampled from 1..9 while board/border marker color is 0,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/27/code.py:80:#    - The output uses a fixed border marker color that never appears inside the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:36:#       - color every displayed dot with the same fixed marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:61:#       component in the input. The fixed marker color only appears in output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:75:#       the solver writes a fixed marker color that is independent of frame\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:76:#       color. The generator reserves this marker color so it is distinct from\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:94:#     positive tallies using the same marker color in the same sample.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:104:#   - A single fixed marker color is easier to infer than a many-to-many color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:107:#   - Reserving the marker color away from every input object prevents false\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:108:#     cues such as distractors sharing the output marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:120:#   - The intended marker color is globally fixed rather than frame-dependent.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:205:    - Use one fixed marker color for all frames instead of reusing each frame's border color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:209:      the quantity is inverted, the placement direction is mirrored, and the marker color is globally shared.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:17:#   If that quadrant matches the marked corner, transfer the source marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:28:#   at least one destination receives a marker color and at least one receives a center color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:387:      - marker color in exactly one corner cell\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:479:    - Compare destination position to that source: if the destination lies in the marker corner's quadrant, copy the