yshev radius from\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:229:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:17:#     and each active marker color is still realized as a diagonal pair of L-corners.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:26:#   - Example: suppose a marker color forms L anchors at TL=(2,4) and BR=(6,9).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:40:#   - Fill colors exclude bg and all legend marker colors so the trail-vs-fill distinction is obvious.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:46:#     one marker color; generator preserves that invariant.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:286:    - Each legend row maps one marker color to one fill color, read from bottom to top.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:287:    - Away from the legend, active marker colors appear as diagonal pairs of L-shaped corners; optional non-legend\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:291:    - For each legend entry, find all non-legend pixels of that marker color and recover the bounding box they define.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/26/code.py:9:#    guides no longer copy the control colors. Instead they use two fixed marker colors:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/26/code.py:56:#    - main() assumes guide marker colors 6 and 8 are absent from the core/fill/frame controls except\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D14/0/code.py:105:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D14/0/code.py:116:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/17/code.py:198:    - For each region, collect marker colors in ascending boundary distance order; if the first marker is not on