wn, one per marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:57:#    - exactly four marker colors and four glyph colors are reused, not expanded;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:58:#    - the body always contains all four marker colors, each at least twice, so\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:74:#    - Because the legend is complete, `main()` assumes each marker color has\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:109:#    `main()` assumes every real marker color has exactly one legend label, the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:177:        assert len(matches) == 1, f\\\"marker color {marker_color} must have exactly one legend label\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:205:    - The body contains single-pixel markers in colors 2, 3, 5, and 8; the same marker colors also\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:209:    - For each marker color, read the 4x4 monochrome sample immediately above-left of its legend label.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:211:      marker color; also confirm that the four learned masks are exactly the four quarter-turn rotations\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/22/code.py:219:      each marker color and which rotation of the puzzle-specific base glyph that marker should use.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/18/code.py:9:#    - Seed task: a border anchor color matches a sprite's rare marker color; top/bottom anchors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/18/code.py:15:#        3) after a sprite moves away, repaint its original 4-neighbor outline in marker color and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/18/code.py:40:#    - Movement assumes one anchor per marker color; generator uses distinct anchor colors and maps\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/18/code.py:57:#    - Trails are monochrome and use the sprite's own marker color, so they clearly read as source\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/18/code.py:81:    - Interior foreground components are sprites with a dominant body color and a rarer marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/18/code.py:85:    - Pair each sprite with the anchor whose color matches its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/18/code.py:87:    - Corner anchors use the marker's larger current offset from the corner to choose the axis: larger column-gap means horizontal motion, otherwise vertical motion. After moving the sprite, repaint its original 4-neighbor boundary cells in the marker color and keep the original marker cell(s) instead of clearing the whole source site.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/5/code.py:14:#      input control row (left to right): `[####][#][###]`, where `#` is a fixed marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/5/code.py:17:#      Each bridge is still painted with the current frame's dot color, not with the control marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/5/code.py:31:#    - A single dedicated control-marker color is used for every run, so the task cannot collapse back into\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/5/code.py:79:#    - `main()` assumes the control row below all frames contains contiguous runs of one marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/30/code.py:71:#   - No new marker colors are introduced beyond the small background palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:31:#   repeated marker colors would mostly create forced collisions. The generator therefore uses\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:41:#   generator can no longer rely on a free alignment axis or on repeated marker colors, so it\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:55:#   The new `main()` assumes the minority color inside each movable sprite is the marker color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:57:#   at most one anchor per marker color and that wrapped placements are collision-free; the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:290:    - Match every sprite to the border anchor that shares its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/14/code.py:15:#     - The base task paints a fixed 4x4 glyph for each marker color and ignores marker position.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/14/code.py:27:#     - The generator always exposes both factors separately: all four marker colors appear inside\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/14/code.py:33:#     - The original solver assumed each marker color owned one final mask. That no longer holds;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/14/code.py:51:#     - The focus marker color appears in all four quadrants, so the learner can also see a single\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/14/code.py:66:#     - main() assumes isolated marker pixels are the only occurrences of marker colors outside the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/14/code.py:237:    - The final orientation is a composition of two visible factors: the marker color tells which\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/27/code.py:17:#    - Original 581f7754 paired a sprite to an anchor by marker color, then stopped exactly\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/27/code.py:29:#      marker ends at column 10. The old task would instead use marker colors and no extra\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/27/code.py:58:#    - Because marker colors never match anchor colors, the old color-based rule is visibly\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/27/code.py:69:#    - They also differ from the source task because no sprite marker color equals any anchor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D3/1/code.py:36:#     - The marker color is fixed and excluded from the TL motif palette so the new cue is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/12/code.py:57:#    - Human solvers can see that marker colors live only on the border while output glyphs appear\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/12/code.py:74:#    - For any marker color, each of the four sides contributes at most one coordinate cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/12/code.py:266:    - Black background with marker colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8 appearing only on the outer border.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/12/code.py:267:    - A top+left pair or a bottom+right pair of the same marker color encodes one glyph top-left coordinate.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/12/code.py:271:    - Reconstruct each placement from its edge pair, then map the marker color to the same fixed glyph alphabet as the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/8/code.py:70:#    - Each sprite still uses only one body color plus one marker color, avoiding clutter despite the extra marker cells.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/8/code.py:100:    - Border anchors are isolated non-background singletons, and their colors match sprite marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/8/code.py:103:    - Pair each sprite with the anchor that shares its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D4/1/code.py:86:# - No hidden color ordering is used. The marker color always matches the cup's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/24/code.py:22:#        1. match a sprite to the anchor sharing its minority marker color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/24/code.py:288:    - Pair each sprite with the anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/1/code.py:16:#       marker color inside a sprite selects an anchor of the same color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/1/code.py:17:#       several sprites may share one marker color and therefore one anchor\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/1/code.py:30:#       even if the largest sprite's marker color is 6 and the first anchor color is 2,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/1/code.py:52:#     separation, so marker colors never match anchor colors at all.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/1/code.py:63:#   - Human solvers can see that there are as many anchors as sprites, that marker colors do\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/1/code.py:87:    - Each sprite has one minority-color marker pixel, but marker colors do not determine which\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/3/code.py:39:    - marker color is fixed and reserved, so humans can read it as a symbol instead of as motif content\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D12/3/code.py:59:    - motif colors exclude the divider and marker colors to reduce clutter\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/3/code.py:570:    - Interior foreground components are mostly multi-color sprites whose least-frequent marker color matches a border anchor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/3/code.py:574:    - Pair each movable sprite with the anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/11/code.py:98:    - Match each sprite to the anchor sharing its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:25:#        * former body pixels are repainted to the anchor/marker color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:66:#    - Input shows three cues at once: body color, minority marker color, and visible border\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:82:#    - Because body colors are chosen distinct from marker colors, every sprite exhibits a real\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:89:#    - It assumes each movable multi-color component has a single minority marker color matched\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:103:    - Interior sprites use one body color plus a rarer marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/7/code.py:107:    - Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/47/code.py:60:#       clean and every piece remains a separate 8-component once marker color is ignored.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/47/code.py:69:#     - background is never a connector color and never the marker color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/47/code.py:214:        assert all(len(m) == 1 for m in marker_comps), \\\"marker color must appear only as singleton pixels\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:16:#    - Every used marker color now has at least one opposite-edge anchor pair:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:316:    - Each marker color has an opposite-edge border-anchor pair, and one color may have extra same-color anchors on the perpendicular border pair as well.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:42:#      was a structure. That fails here because valid movers contain both red and a marker color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/15/code.py:69:#    - Every valid moving piece has exactly one non-red marker color, and that color is equal to\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/15/code.py:21:#      1. match each sprite to the anchor of the same marker color;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/15/code.py:27:#         marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/15/code.py:35:#    - The trail color is exactly the marker color; this keeps the extra visual language small and legible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/15/code.py:634:    - Match each sprite to the anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/15/code.py:637:    - On its turn, remove only that sprite, step toward the target line until the next step would leave the grid or hit any non-background cell, paste the sprite there, and paint the marker's traversed cells as a one-cell-wide trail in the marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/16/code.py:36:#    - \\\"control is monochrome\\\" is false: it now has body color + marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/2/code.py:16:#   Each anchor still matches sprites by marker color, but it no longer chooses a single slide\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/2/code.py:23:#   (1,2). Suppose a sprite with marker color 4 starts with its marker at (7,8).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/2/code.py:259:    - Isolated border singletons act as anchors, and a sprite is paired to the anchor with the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/16/code.py:29:#    The generator keeps 2-3 anchor colors and 4-5 sprites so marker colors repeat and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/16/code.py:54:#    A human looking at a few examples can spot that marker colors still match anchors,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/16/code.py:60:#    even when several sprites share a marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/16/code.py:82:    - Match each sprite to the anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/7/code.py:21:#    1. First infer the marker color as the unique least-frequent non-background\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/7/code.py:56:#    Across examples, the marker color changes and is not red, but is always the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/7/code.py:58:#    pixels of the same color remain, making both \\\"identify the marker color\\\" and\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/7/code.py:222:    marker color, erase only true marker pixels, and keep same-color decoys.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/7/code.py:433:    - marker color is non-red and uniquely least frequent in the input,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:51:#       marker color as the handle that must reach the crossing.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/9/code.py:123:    - Each moving sprite is a 2-color component whose minority marker color matches one center pixel; only that marker lies on the rail.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/0/code.py:37:#    - Only one new symbol is introduced: marker color 8.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/0/code.py:70:#    - The marker color is constant and structurally attached to the basin walls, so the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/0/code.py:75:#      marker color. The marker reuses wall cells rather than floating in open air, so it\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/10/code.py:97:    - Match each multicolor sprite to the border anchor with the same marker color, then compute the one-axis translation that aligns the marker with that anchor row or column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:19:#    frequent color is a marker. Each sprite slides toward the anchor of the same marker color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:35:#    That keeps the hidden state small enough to infer while still making \\\"same marker color moves\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:59:#    settles second, while matching sprites of the same marker color move together.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:66:#    marker colors are used, reducing ambiguity about which group is earlier.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:73:#    main() assumes each marker color maps to exactly one anchor and that grouped clearing never\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:75:#    marker color and keeps input components non-overlapping.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:269:    - Match each movable component to the unique anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/21/code.py:271:    - Components sharing one marker color move together, different marker colors are processed in ascending color order, and each group's translated pixels overwrite whatever is currently present; later groups therefore cover earlier groups, while pixels pushed out of bounds are clipped.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:18:#    a sprite marker color 4 matched the unique border anchor color 4.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:22:#    marker colors rather than the anchor colors themselves.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:41:#    - Color equality no longer identifies the anchor; marker colors must be translated via legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:53:#    in one corner; the same anchor colors appear in both halves; and the sprite marker colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:55:#    a human can see both that \\\"same marker color can live in both halves\\\" and that the border\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:59:#    Body colors avoid both backgrounds, the legend frame, and all semantic anchor/marker colors,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:75:    - One corner contains a framed legend whose inner rows encode [anchor color, marker color].\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:76:    - Outside the legend, isolated border pixels are anchors and interior sprites carry the marker colors from the legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:80:    - For each sprite, use its own region plus its marker color to identify the matching border anchor in that same region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/19/code.py:83:    Key insight: Neither color cue is sufficient alone: the legend translates marker colors into anchor colors, and the repeated anchor colors are disambiguated by the sprite's background partition.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:19:#      sprites whose least-frequent color is the marker. Matching is still by marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:24:#        top-edge anchor color 4 at column 3, input marker color 4 at (5,6).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:31:#    - Use the marker color itself for the trail; this makes the correspondence visible without adding\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:64:#    - Because trail color equals marker color and each sample repeats colors across multiple sprites,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:98:    - Isolated non-background border singletons are anchors, and anchor colors match sprite marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:101:    - Pair each sprite with the anchor of the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:103:    - Instead of moving toward the anchor, the sprite moves the same distance away from it, then the cleared source marker path is redrawn as a continuous trail in the marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/37/code.py:19:#    - D9 changes \\\"what counts\\\" in the controls: only one echoed marker color per control matters.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/37/code.py:20:#      UL's marker color is the unique non-black color it shares with LL. UR's marker color is the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/37/code.py:31:#    - Each control quadrant has exactly one echoed marker color and at least one distractor pixel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/37/code.py:279:    Infer the two control marker colors from palette echoes, then cross-map those counts into the output size.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/28/code.py:410:    - Match each movable sprite to the anchor with the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/13/code.py:57:#    - Original matching key was just marker color. That is no longer sufficient because two\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/29/code.py:33:#     - the set of border-marker colors is the \\\"allowed colors\\\" legend\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/23/code.py:65:    - Isolated non-background border pixels are anchors; each anchor color matches the marker color of the sprites it controls.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/23/code.py:68:    - Match each movable component to the anchor with the same marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/22/code.py:13:#   - Original task: irregular bodies with a side-attached marker were moved by matching marker color to a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/22/code.py:180:    - Each movable multicolor sprite is one 8-connected component made of a solid rectangle body plus one 1-pixel marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/22/code.py:184:    - Pair every sprite with the border anchor sharing its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/6/code.py:21:- Base task: a special marker color defines a row axis, a column axis, or a point\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/6/code.py:25:  2. Infer the marker color by counting all non-background cells in the whole\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/6/code.py:61:  2. The marker color is the unique least-frequent non-background color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/6/code.py:78:- Humans can see that the marker is not fixed red because the marker color varies\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/6/code.py:132:        raise ValueError(\\\"marker color is not uniquely least frequent\\\")\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/6/code.py:19:#    - Each interior sprite still has a large body color and a rarer marker color, but the marker is now a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/6/code.py:110:      marker color; the marker cells form a 2-3 cell straight segment.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/30/code.py:28:#    - Base task logic is preserved: each interior sprite has a rare marker color that matches one isolated\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/30/code.py:243:    - Match each movable sprite to the anchor sharing its marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D1/3/code.py:42:#      That assumption is removed; slot choice is now read from marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D1/3/code.py:190:    - For each outer slot, read its marker color and copy in the surrounding 3x3\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D1/3/code.py:194:    The marker colors create a color-to-block lookup, so destination slots must be\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db0c5428/D1/3/code.py:229:                    \\\"reused marker colors require identical source blocks\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/14/code.py:56:#      frame; same-looking small hollow sprites with unmatched marker colors do not move.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/14/code.py:81:#      winning marker color has no border anchor. The generator constructs exactly that.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/14/code.py:91:    - Extra small hollow sprites use the same pattern, but their topological marker color does not appear among the border anchors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/12/code.py:69:    - Read each sprite's marker color from that topmost/leftmost pixel and match it to the secondary-ring anchor of the same color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/1/code.py:13:#      the hole's surrounding outline pixels into the same marker color. The copied color is still\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/1/code.py:14:#      the cavity's main fill color, but the correspondence is now \\\"marker color match\\\" rather\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/1/code.py:32:#      Here each component is \\\"majority fill color + one minority marker color\\\", so the solver\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/1/code.py:79:    Fill each `dst` hole with the main fill color of the `src` cavity whose marker color matches\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/25/code.py:34:#      the river. No extra marker colors are introduced.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/7/code.py:14:#         outline. Equal marker colors define the pairing, so geometry no longer decides\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/7/code.py:30:#      4 unique marker colors + 2 repeated src fill colors + 2 mapped legend colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/7/code.py:52:#    - The marker colors each appear exactly twice across the input, once on src and once\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/7/code.py:76:#    - Each src cavity has exactly one unique marker color and one majority fill color;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/7/code.py:92:    Pair src cavities to dst holes by marker color, then recolor via a legend before filling.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/48/code.py:20:    不能 4 邻接。图例本身要从拼图碎片里剔除，避免污染面积、组件和 frame 检测。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:16:#         every source subsprite cell is rewritten to one uniform marker color\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:27:#    - The marker color is a single reserved color for the whole sample, not a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:38:#      the absolute source fill pixels so it can rewrite them to the marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:66:#      become the same marker color. This is easy to spot from 2-3 samples.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:70:#    - The grey marker color is absent from the input palette. Generator reserves color 5.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/16/code.py:335:    rewrite all src subsprite pixels to one marker color to show that the colors were\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/30/code.py:26:#        * one outside-marker color, visible on the tile border\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/30/code.py:27:#        * one inside-marker color, visible only inside a closed boundary\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/30/code.py:88:#    - Every generated sample must differ from the original overlay rule because both marker colors are\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/30/code.py:97:#      one enclosed region of a single marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/30/code.py:98:#      Guarantee: `_make_semantic_template` fills the whole exterior with one marker color and the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/30/code.py:99:#      interior with another marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/30/code.py:284:    - The lower-right quadrant is a fully non-black multicolor template containing one outside marker color, one inside marker color, and one or two preserved structure colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/30/code.py:39:#       marker pixels are introduced, so the new solver must identify and erase marker colors before\\n/ho