ew/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/6/code.py:17:#    a small pool. This prevents a trivial \\\"hole marker color == fill color\\\" shortcut.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/24/code.py:10:#    - The original task used color 1 as the dedicated T-marker color, so any color-1 cell was guaranteed to be\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/24/code.py:23:#    - Only two rotation colors are used, and only one T-marker color is used, so the solver still reasons over a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/14/code.py:112:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Infer the marker color as repeated singleton components each touching one object.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/1/code.py:184:    - Away from the legend, each marker color appears either as two opposite L-corners of a bbox or as a solid 2x2 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/1/code.py:188:    - Read legend entries from bottom to top and collect the non-legend pixels of that marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D5/0/code.py:165:      diagonal location; that marker color is the glyph color for that destination.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D5/0/code.py:170:    - Paint the same glyph, rotated to each destination corner, in that destination's marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:16:#     - Each active marker color still appears either as one L-pair on a bbox diagonal or as one solid 2x2 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:32:#     - Fill colors are kept different from bg and from every legend marker color so payload pixels cannot be misread as another marker object.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:44:#     - Every non-noop L entry gets interior payload in the legend's fill color, so the output clearly shows those cells changing to the marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:127:    Swap marker color with fill color inside diagonal marker constructions using a color legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:131:    - Away from the legend, each marker color appears either as an L-shaped diagonal corner pair or as a solid 2x2 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:135:    - Read legend entries bottom-to-top and locate all non-legend pixels of that marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/3/code.py:137:    - Recolor every current marker pixel to the legend fill color; inside the target diamond, pre-existing non-background pixels become the marker color, while remaining background cells become the fill color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/2/code.py:129:    - Each legend row gives a marker color and its paired output color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/2/code.py:130:    - Away from the legend, each marker color appears either as two diagonal L-corners or as one solid 2x2 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D5/2/code.py:133:    - Read legend entries from bottom to top and gather all non-legend pixels of that marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D9/1/code.py:29:#      corner/inward part uses the target's own marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D9/1/code.py:215:      source color, head cells use the target marker color. The target's marker\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D9/1/code.py:219:    - The target's own marker color does not simply fill the whole glyph. It\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/1/code.py:96:#   the unique non-marker color 4-adjacent to blue; every blob patch preserves\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/29/code.py:113:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/29/code.py:125:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/c