olor, exactly as in the original task.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D1/3/code.py:220:      diagonal cell; that marker color is the target's output color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D1/3/code.py:226:    - Paint the rotated glyph using the target corner's own marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D1/3/code.py:230:    reflection while still reusing the visible marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/26/code.py:484:    assert colors, \\\"expected foreground line and marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/26/code.py:495:    assert marker_colors, \\\"expected singleton marker colors\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/26/code.py:525:    - Non-marker colors form one-cell-thick horizontal and vertical stroke fragments that may logically cross.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/0/code.py:142:    - Each legend row maps a marker color to a fill color, read from bottom to top.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/0/code.py:146:    - Scan the legend bottom-to-top and gather all non-legend pixels of the current marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D9/0/code.py:148:    - Otherwise treat the marker bbox as a TL-BR anchored L-pair and fill the opposite TR-BL diamond, while protecting legend cells, current marker pixels, and later marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D1/2/code.py:43:#   that marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D1/2/code.py:63:# - Colors still behave exactly as in the original: each target uses its own marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c416de3/D1/2/code.py:194:      sign flips, and paint it with the target corner's marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/31/code.py:332:    - Red and/or yellow marker colors are exactly the foreground colors whose 4-connected components are all singleton pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu