/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:37:#   endpoint changes back to marker color. That difference is directly visible in\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:79:      marker color; bystanders are not changed.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:83:    ray, lends its color to the track, and receives the marker color in return.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:18:#       The left cell is the output color; the right cell is the marker color to look for around sprite holes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:37:#       hole rims and unique marker colors in the legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:44:#       marker color hugging holes inside sprites. The marker sits exactly where the legend says to look.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:183:        assert marker not in mapping, \\\"legend marker colors must be unique\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:216:    - In every pair, the left cell gives the target output color and the right cell gives the marker color to match.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:217:    - Interior sprites are connected blobs made of grey plus one marker color painted on cells that touch enclosed holes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:488:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Recolor all hole-adjacent sprite cells with the marker color.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:8:#      either fill the full beat with the marker color, or fill one bounded span\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:44:#      cells that are still bg or the original marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:113:        f\\\"marker color: {dict(colors)}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:140:            f\\\"Line {line} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) non-marker color {col} \\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:9:#    - The non-legend area now contains several disconnected objects of that single marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:20:#        Therefore the new solver must split the marker color into connected components first,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:26:#    - All objects share one marker color and one fill color; this is the visible signature of D10.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:30:#    - `for ... in entries` previously assumed one marker color per object family. With one legend row,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:53:#    - Because the same marker color is reused across multiple objects, a solver can infer that the legend\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:211:    - The bottom-left legend is exactly one 2-cell row: marker color in the left cell, fill color in the right cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:212:    - Outside the legend, the same marker color appears in several disconnected objects.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:217:    - Split all non-legend pixels of that marker color into small connected pieces.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:296:# 3. All non-legend marker objects share the legend marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:46:#      but the generator must ensure at most one aligned non-marker color per line.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:52:#   grouped marker color and at most one extra single pixel. The bars are isolated\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:85:    - Each active line contains exactly one repeating marker color, represented by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:93:    - On each active line, detect the unique marker color by its two equal runs:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:101:      marker color. With a companion, also recolor both marker bars to the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:14:#     - Each legend row is (marker color, fill color), read bottom -> top.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:26:#       - The solver still reads those rows bottom -> top and processes each marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:35:#     - Using 6-8 entries is already near the ARC palette limit because marker colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:44:#     - main() groups all non-legend pixels of one marker color into one object. Therefore\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:45:#       each legend marker color must correspond to exactly one placed marker group or be\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:49:#     - main() protects future marker colors by legend order. With 6-8 rows this becomes\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:166:    - Each legend row stores a marker color in the left cell and its fill color in the right cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:167:    - Elsewhere, each marker color appears either as one diagonal pair of L-corners or as one solid 2x2 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:171:    - For an L-pair, collect that marker color's non-legend pixels, find which diagonal holds the L-anchors,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:387:    \\\"\\\"\\\"Create the legend grid, rows, mask, and marker colors.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:37:#     mover's marker color. This is strong enough to see, but not so unconstrained that examples\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:44:#     Fix: collect row/col marks by marker color, then translate marker -> sprite main color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:59:#   - Edge marker colors do not appear as source main colors, so the legend is necessary.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:60:#   - The source accent color is shared, but output accent cells become each mover's marker color,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:139:    - row 0: marker colors\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:20:#     4-5 legend rows, and 2-3 of those rows are decoys: their marker color appears\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:42:#     is valid only if the marker color appears outside the legend. That remains the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:46:#     guarantee that noop rows have no stray pixels of their marker color elsewhere.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:47:#   - Future-marker protection still works because marker colors remain distinct even\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:152:    - The lower-left corner contains a vertical 2-column legend; each row pairs a marker color with its fill color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:153:    - Away from the legend, some marker colors appear as opposite L-corners of a bounding box, and some appear as a solid 2x2 block.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:154:    - In this variant, several legend rows are deliberate decoys: their marker color never appears outside the legend at all.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:157:    - Read legend rows from bottom to top and inspect each marker color independently.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/2/code.py:463:    # D10 guarantee: the marker colors of noop legend rows must not appear outside the legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D3/2/code.py:44:#    - Old endpoint extraction read colors from ring-touch cells. Those cells no longer carry the marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a6f40cea/D3/2/code.py:225:    - Same-color pairs yield a solid L, while two-color pairs yield an alternating L whose elbow keeps the inner marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:29:#       pixel outside the legend now uses one of the legend marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:49:#     - `main()` collects all non-legend pixels of a legend marker color into one object.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:51:#       safe here because the variant forbids any extra non-legend marker colors entirely.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:62:#       lacks a legend row. Every foreground marker color appears in the legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:157:    - Outside the legend, every foreground marker pixel belongs to one of those legend marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:161:    - For each legend row, gather all non-legend pixels of that marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:170:      every visible marker color directly corresponds to a legend entry.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/0/code.py:394:    \\\"\\\"\\\"All non-legend foreground pixels must use one of the legend marker colors.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/1/code.py:14:# - Concrete behavior: the legend at bottom-left is still the only source of valid marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/1/code.py:21:#   legend-listed marker colors; all three fake pairs remain unchanged in the output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D11/1/code.py:29:#   a legend marker color, so generator reserves distractor colors outside the legend marker set.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385b