/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D2/1/code.py:192:        assert marker_color in mapping, f\\\"missing legend for marker color {marker_color}\\\"\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/1/code.py:156:    - For each region, sort marker colors by boundary depth; if the shallowest marker is not on the boundary, insert the base color at the front.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/1/code.py:159:    Key insight: Marker depth still defines the palette order, but the trajectory is no longer periodic; the innermost marker color absorbs the entire remaining core instead of restarting the palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/1/code.py:185:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D19/0/code.py:50:#   Only three output marker colors carry meaning: grey=safe shooter, maroon=hit sprite or lone bg\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D12/0/code.py:227:    - For every non-wall region, sort marker colors by boundary depth; if no depth-0 marker exists, prepend the region base color, then paint cyclic concentric frames with that palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D12/0/code.py:258:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D12/0/code.py:373:      - used: set of marker colors used\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D4/1/code.py:117:    - For each marker color, read the 4x4 sample just above-left of its legend label to learn that marker's glyph mask.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D6/1/code.py:151:    - The marker colors still select from a fixed glyph alphabet; the only new behavior is that glyph coordinates live on a wraparound surface rather than a clipped rectangle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/2/code.py:49:#       - Use only 0-3 markers per region and 3-9 distinct marker colors grid-wide, which\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/2/code.py:148:    - For each region, read ma