fine the repeating palette by\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D4/1/code.py:252:    - For each region, sort the singleton marker colors by Chebyshev distance from that region's outer boundary.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D4/1/code.py:286:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:28:#    marker-bearing regions and uses globally unique marker colors, so the global\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:36:#    collect marker colors globally before processing region fill.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:124:    - Gather all marker colors across the entire grid in row-major order, keeping the first occurrence of each color to form one global palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:225:#   globally distinct marker colors to keep that order unambiguous and visible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D2/2/code.py:87:    - Azure background with blue diamond/octagon blobs; green edge pixels mark each blob's outgoing port side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/1/code.py:19:#    - The glyph dictionary itself is unchanged: marker color still chooses one fixed 4x4 boolean mask and one\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/1/code.py:53:#    - Solver assumptions are matched by construction: for each marker color there is at most one top, bottom,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/1/code.py:57:#    - Across examples, marker colors are absent from the interior and appear only on the border. Human solvers can\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/1/code.py:196:    - Black background with marker colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8 appearing only on the outer border.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D3/1/code.py:197:    - A top+left pair or bottom+right pair of the same marker color encodes one glyph top-left coordinate.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D