tte_length].\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/1/code.py:236:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/2/code.py:18:#   marker colors as the palette source, but the geometry now starts from the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/2/code.py:20:#   radius 1, and so on. To preserve multiple marker colors instead of collapsing\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/2/code.py:33:#   the same palette entry and make later marker colors visually weak. The chosen\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/2/code.py:34:#   nearest-marker rule keeps 2-3 distinct marker colors active in each marked\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/2/code.py:129:    - For every region, collect marker colors in reading order to form a cyclic palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D10/2/code.py:195:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/2/code.py:25:#    also recolors one wall cell near a region with one of that region's marker colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/2/code.py:277:    - Some wall pixels are recolored as tiny symbols; each such wall dot repeats one marker color from a neighboring region.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/2/code.py:280:    - For every region, sort its internal marker colors by boundary distance, and prepend the base color if the first marker begins deeper than distance 0.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/2/code.py:281:    - If an adjacent wall symbol matches one of that region's marker colors, rotate that palette so the matching color becomes the first band color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D15/2/code.py:306:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D6/0/code.py:161:    - Inside that region, build the palette exactly as in the original task: order marker colors by bound